**How each security goal is met:**

| Goal | Mechanism |
|---|---|
| Tokens cannot be forged / guessed / altered | HMAC-SHA-256 over the payload, keyed with the server `secret`; 128-bit random nonce per issuance |
| Foreign-`secret` tokens rejected | Verification recomputes the HMAC with *this* handler's `secret`; a mismatch fails `crypto.subtle.verify` |
| 1-hour expiry | `now().getTime() >= t + 3 600 000` at every authenticated request (no timers) |
| Logout revocation | The full token string is inserted into the `revoked` `Set`; the check happens before HMAC verification |
| Members blocked from admin routes | `user.role !== "admin"` → 403 on `/admin/stats` |
| No user enumeration | Login returns the same `401 invalid_credentials` for unknown username *and* wrong password |
| No password / secret leakage | Token payload carries only `username`, `issuedAt`, and a random nonce; the secret appears only as the HMAC key |
| Unique tokens | 128 bits of `crypto.getRandomValues` per login make collisions infeasible even at the same millisecond |

